        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"sand-la-mare-au-diable-29846ede358130e4\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.94,\"analysis\":\"The embedded “je t’aime” presents Germain’s love as a true inner state supposedly legible in his eyes. The personification of his eyes emphasizes visible evidence and sincerity, not a commitment undertaken by the words or a reflex-like verbal discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The declaration occurs during marriage-oriented courtship, but that context alone does not give the embedded love proposition substantial performative force.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"nonverbal_verbalised\",\"description\":\"Germain directly speaks the sentence, but the embedded “je t’aime” is metaphorically attributed to his eyes as a nonverbal disclosure: “Mes yeux te disent que je t’aime.”\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Germain is seeking Marie’s response after having been encouraged to ask her to marry him. He portrays his gaze as unmistakable evidence of a love he has already verbally acknowledged. His anxious courtship and the later revelation that Marie reciprocates support a sincere avowal, while the surrounding marriage proposal remains contextual rather than converting this embedded clause into an undertaking.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Mes yeux te disent que je t’aime. Regarde-moi donc dans les yeux, ça y est écrit” (“My eyes tell you that I love you. Look into my eyes; it is written there”).\",\"supports\":\"Strong truth-conditional force: Germain presents love as an existing state visibly disclosed by his gaze.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Immediately beforehand Germain says that if Marie could change her mind, he would be very happy; Marie asks whether it is settled that he loves her.\",\"supports\":\"The utterance answers uncertainty about Germain’s feelings and therefore functions principally as an avowal.\",\"confidence\":0.96},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The conversation was prompted by Germain being told to ask Marie to marry him, but the highlighted wording itself describes what his eyes reveal.\",\"supports\":\"Explains the courtship setting while limiting performative support: marriage is discussed around the utterance, not undertaken by the embedded “je t’aime.”\",\"confidence\":0.94},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The narration later says Germain speaks “comme dans un rêve sans entendre ce qu’il disait,” but this description occurs during his subsequent extended speech rather than specifically at the highlighted sentence.\",\"supports\":\"Emotional absorption is present in the scene, but there is insufficient evidence that producing the highlighted words is itself a reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.88},{\"evidence_id\":\"e5\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is marked as an affirmative present-tense, main-or-embedded instance and retained as a valid explicit love-I-you occurrence.\",\"supports\":\"Confirms that the embedded clause is an explicit affirmative love predication rather than an incidental lexical match.\",\"confidence\":0.99}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the avowal of an existing loving state. The metaphorical nonverbal framing and courtship circumstances are adequately represented through utterance status and context; they create no residual need for E, P, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
